{title: That's Rock & Roll}
{artist: Shaun Cassidy}
{key: G}
{tempo: 120}
{duration: 3:45}

{start_of_part: Intro}
[G]
{end_of_part}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Well, I was sixteen and sick of [D]school, I
didn't [G]know what I wanted to [C]do.
I bought a [G]guitar, I got the [C]fever..[D]that's
rock 'n' [G]roll.[D]
I played at [G]parties, played in [D]bars, I spent
my [G]money buyin' new [C]guitars.
I screamed my [G]heart out but how I [C]loved it.[D].that's
 rock 'n' roll.[G][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Well, come on everybody get [C]down and get [D]with it.
[G]Come on everybody get [C]down and get [D]with it.
[G]Come on everybody get [C]down, that's [D]rock 'n' [G]roll[D].
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
It's when [G]smoking up and the [D]heat have got your
[G]heart pounding right with the [C]beat.
Don't try to [G]fight it, just get [C]excited, [D]that's
rock 'n' [G]roll.[D]
Now, don't you [G]worry 'bout bein' a [D]star, it
doesn't [G]matter who or what you [C]are.
Just get the [G]rhythm, and let it [C]fill ya, [D]that's
rock 'n' [G]roll.[D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Well, come on everybody get [C]down and get [D]with it.
[G]Come on everybody get [C]down and get [D]with it.
[G]Come on everybody get [C]down, that's [D]rock 'n' [G]roll[D].
{end_of_chorus}

